| T<n> | RDP audio | brainstorm | prod-codex, prod-fable | — | — | round 1: independent drafts | — | operator 2026-09-28: "Now the RDP audio thing — I want a design by morning. Go." | no |
```

```bash
# Bash, foreground
bash orchestrator/build-backlog.sh
```

Artifact tool: republish to the same page path. Then in chat:

> **Now.** The WireGuard keepalive relay (the small nginx server on the gateway that passes the VPN client's "I am alive" request to Pritunl) is accepted on ccs-it. I am closing the task: the live-state snapshot of ccs-it, the design and plan marked implemented, then cleanup. RDP audio is in the backlog as T\<n\> at "brainstorm", the design stage: two product advisors (Codex and Claude) each draft independently, criticise each other's draft and merge them into one document; the two voting advisors decide every open question, then approve it.
> **Next.** The design reaches you as an Artifact with a sign-off poll (hard rule #9). No executor starts before that. No round is shortened to hit the morning: an advisor split, or a question only you can answer, waits for you as a poll. If the full process cannot make the morning, you get a poll about that, not a thinner design.
> **You.** Answer the one poll that follows.
